      "created_at": "2018-10-15T22:45:58Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-10-15T22:45:58Z",
      "body": "Quick summary from Slack (without details because this is a public issue)\r\n\r\n- Only about 30 paid or grassroots deployments use Twitter at all\r\n- Once we ignore draft posts, it gets down to just 6 deployments with a handful of posts\r\n- Unpaid deployments will get archived if they don't upgrade soon\r\n\r\nI think this means that a lot of the issue with old Twitter data will go away once free (aka basic) deployments start getting turned off when they don't upgrade.\r\n\r\nFor the remainder of them:\r\n- Those we own, we could clean out the twitter data manually if needed\r\n- The others we could reach out to and ask if we can remove twitter posts\r\n\r\nThe easiest solution then for new deployments would be to disable the Twitter data source entirely. ",
